# RDF Unreleased Release Notes

## Unreleased

-- New Features --

[New] rdf tokens reports cache rebuilds: turns after an idle gap past the cache TTL (5 min, or
      1 h when the turn's 1h writes exceed its 5m writes) that rewrite at least half of a 50K+
      token context, costed as the write price minus a cache read; --json adds a rebuilds object,
      --summary rebuild_events and rebuild_cost_usd, and the text report a cache rebuilds line
[New] read discipline: reference/read-discipline.md ladder (locate first; read whole under 400
      lines; map or a 200-250 line window above; a whole large file only when editing or
      reviewing across it) with LSP code intelligence use and limits; planner, engineer, qa and
      reviewer carry the rule and list LSP in their tools
[New] rdf doctor harness: subagent prompt cache TTL check; WARNs when subagents run on the
      automatic 5m TTL and recommends "subagentPromptCacheTtl": "1h" in ~/.claude/settings.json,
      resolving CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_PROMPT_CACHE_TTL, then the setting, then ENABLE_PROMPT_CACHING_1H

-- Changes --

[Change] mutation checks run only the tests that target the mutated code, then the full suite
         once: engineer red step, reviewer regression pass, core governance template, CLAUDE.md,
         and a "Mutation checks" section with the filter command in each language testing reference
[Change] read thresholds 500 -> 400 lines: /r-util-code-map default, /r-audit large-file
         discipline, /r-init convention ingest; core governance Context Window Hygiene and
         CLAUDE.md.ref Context Preservation carry the ladder

-- Bug Fixes --

[Fix] docs site: the 3.9.1 em dash sweep left an unquoted colon in docs/_config.yml, so Pages
      builds failed from 3.9.1 on; the description is quoted again
[Fix] /r-audit told reviewer subagents to invoke /r-util-code-map, a skill subagents cannot
      call; they now map large files inline (LSP documentSymbol or a definitions grep)
